  "application_type_full": "Full planning & demolition in a conservation area",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of the demolition of the existing dwelling, which makes a positive contribution to the character and appearance of the Grange Park Conservation Area, and its replacement with a dwelling of insufficient architectural quality, design merit, and sensitivity to its historic context, would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Conservation Area. The harm caused is not outweighed by any public benefits and therefore the proposal is contrary to sections 16(2) and 72(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Section 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy HC1 of the London Plan 2021, Policies 30, and 31 of the Core Strategy 2010, and Policies DMD8, DMD37 and DMD44 of the Development Management Document 2014."
  ],
